Why Do Both Models Exist?

• OSI is used as a teaching and troubleshooting tool. Network engineers still say things like "It's a Layer 2 issue" (meaning a switch or cable problem) or "Check Layer 3" (meaning an IP or router problem) because the 7 layers make it easy to pinpoint where something broke.
• TCP/IP is the actual rulebook built into every phone, laptop, and router on Earth.
